From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ori Shalom <ori.100000@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:12:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix: give Chromium a quarantine service for downloads and
 saved files

Chromium marks a completed download, and a file the File System Access
API writes, through the embedder's quarantine service connection
(DownloadManagerDelegate and ContentBrowserClient
GetQuarantineConnectionCallback). Electron overrode neither, so outside
Windows, where Chromium writes the Mark of the Web itself without one,
such files got no quarantine attribute: on macOS no
com.apple.quarantine, so Gatekeeper never checked them when opened.

Connect both to a quarantine service in the browser process, as Chrome
does outside Windows (ChromeDownloadManagerDelegate::
ConnectToQuarantineService). On macOS that also records where the file
came from (kMDItemWhereFroms and the quarantine event's URLs). Windows
keeps Chromium's direct Mark of the Web.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
